    "finalText": "Implementation complete and verified. Summary of what's in place:\n\n- **Rails 8.0.2 API-only app** (pinned exactly; also pinned `json` to 2.9.1 since json 3.x broke Rails 8.0.2's `quirks_mode` JSON calls)\n- **`app/models/link.rb`** — Active Record validations: absolute http/https URL with host, code format `[A-Za-z0-9_-]{4,20}`, unique code (DB index + race-safe 409), auto-generated `SecureRandom` code when omitted\n- **`app/controllers/links_controller.rb`** — create (201/409/422), show (200/404), index (ascending creation order, `items`+`total`), redirect (302 with exact `Location`, atomic single click increment, 404 JSON); malformed JSON rescued to 422 with `error`\n- **`config/database.yml`** — reads `DATABASE_URL` from the environment, no hard-coded credentials\n- **`start.sh`** (executable) — `bin/rails db:prepare` then foreground server on `0.0.0.0:8000`\n- **README** — \"Starting the server\" section\n\nVerified with an 86-check HTTP suite (all passing), plus: data and click counts surviving a server restart, pending migrations applied by `start.sh` (rolled back and re-applied), and a clean cold boot. The test database is empty and port 8000 is free for the harness."
